From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:22:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Allow the plugin id to be set at build time

LuneOS registers the plugin as "prpl-discord": imlibpurpleservice, the
Discord account template and the accounts already stored on devices use
that id. Guard the default DISCORD_PLUGIN_ID with #ifndef so the recipe
can set it from a force-included header instead of patching the source.

Upstream declined this in #498: the id should not change. So this stays
a LuneOS patch.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [webOS specific]
---
 libdiscord.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libdiscord.c b/libdiscord.c
index b03f5d4..89b431f 100644
--- a/libdiscord.c
+++ b/libdiscord.c
@@ -58,7 +58,9 @@
 #define purple_ssl_read(a, b, c)  ((a) && (a)->private_data ? purple_ssl_read((a), (b), (c)) : 0)
 
 #ifndef DISCORD_PLUGIN_OVERRIDE
+#ifndef DISCORD_PLUGIN_ID
 #define DISCORD_PLUGIN_ID "prpl-eionrobb-discord"
+#endif
 #define DISCORD_PLUGIN_NAME "Discord"
 #ifndef DISCORD_PLUGIN_VERSION
 #define DISCORD_PLUGIN_VERSION "1.0"
